<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Girolamo Durazzo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1739–1809</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Girolamo Luigi Durazzo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Girolamo Luigi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durres">Durazzo</a> was a Genoese nobleman and politician of the Durazzo family, one of the leading houses of the old Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genoa">Genoa</a>. Under the constitution of 1802 he became the only doge of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ligurian-republic">Ligurian Republic</a>, a French client state. His term ended in 1805, when the republic was annexed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-colonial-empire">French Empire</a>.</p></div>
